cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite as below."
title: "Indus script: machine-readable seal catalogues from Mackay (1938) and Marshall (1931), with photo-coded text features and a reproducible analysis pipeline"
abstract: "Two machine-readable catalogues of Mohenjo-daro seals with find-spots and levels, transcribed from page images by an AI model (Mackay (1938): independent Tesseract OCR cross-check, on 596 of 709 rows, agreement 95.7% on type; depth and field number not independently verified; Marshall (1931): independent Tesseract OCR cross-check, agreement 97.5% on type, 96.4% on area, 76.7% on serial); text features coded from all thirteen of Mackay's seal plates; a held-out validated constraint set on Indus sign sequences; and a reproducible pipeline of genre- and size-matched structural comparisons against Sumerian, Egyptian, Aegean and proto-cuneiform corpora. Results are mainly negative and documented as such. No decipherment is offered."
authors:
